# SonoJS folder structure

Group related files **by item** (component, block, chart, example set, docs page). Do not dump many sibling files flat in a shared folder when they belong to one named item.

## Registry

```
registry/
  examples/
    button/
      default.tsx
      outline.tsx
      sizes.tsx
      index.ts          # re-exports for the set
  blocks/
    login-01/
      page.tsx
      components/
        login-form.tsx
  charts/
    chart-area/
      chart-area.tsx
      index.ts
```

UI components: author in `packages/ui/src/components/` only (`registry:build` → `public/r/`).

Rules:

1. **One folder per item name** (`button`, `login-01`, `chart-area`). Folder name matches the registry / docs slug.
2. **Examples** live under `registry/examples/<component>/`, not `registry/examples/<component>-<variant>.tsx` at the root of `examples/`.
3. **Blocks / charts** already use (or must use) a dedicated folder; keep all files for that item inside it.
4. Prefer a small `index.ts` barrel when the folder has multiple entry files consumers import together.
5. Shared utilities stay in `lib/`, `hooks/`, or `packages/ui/src/lib` — not inside a random component folder unless they are private to that item.

## `@sonojs/ui` package

```
packages/ui/src/
  components/
    button.tsx              # single-file OK
    sidebar.tsx             # or sidebar/ if it grows multi-file
  hooks/
  lib/
  styles/
```

- Default: one file per component under `components/`.
- If a component needs helpers, subcomponents, or tests, promote to `components/<name>/` with `index.ts` as the public entry.

## Docs app

```
app/(app)/docs/components/<name>/page.tsx
app/(app)/docs/<topic>/page.tsx
```

Docs for a component live under that component’s folder, not as loose files under `docs/components/`.

## Site chrome (`components/`)

**Rule:** if a feature needs **more than one file**, put it in `components/<feature>/` with an `index.ts` barrel. Do not leave related siblings flat next to unrelated chrome.

Current groups:

```
components/
  docs/           # ComponentSource, CopyButton, variant preview, API props
  direction/      # DirectionProvider + DirectionToggle
  site-header/    # header, main-nav, mobile-nav, mode-switcher
  sidebar-nav/    # docs/charts/blocks sidebars + shared nav UI/search
  theme-provider.tsx          # single-file OK
  site-footer.tsx             # single-file OK
  scroll-to-top.tsx           # single-file OK
  …
```

Single-file utilities may stay flat. The moment a second related file appears, promote to a folder.

## Checklist (new item)

